WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.858
Slop University is an artwork.

00:00:03.358 --> 00:00:08.373
It is a fictional institution: a working university that has never taught anyone anything.

00:00:09.373 --> 00:00:17.036
Its research outputs, press releases, researcher profiles and identifiers are generated by an autonomous software pipeline,

00:00:17.336 --> 00:00:19.054
that runs on a timer.

00:00:20.054 --> 00:00:24.141
A capable language model can satisfy every proxy the sector counts:

00:00:24.441 --> 00:00:25.184
an output,

00:00:25.384 --> 00:00:26.312
a crest,

00:00:26.512 --> 00:00:27.256
a DOI,

00:00:27.456 --> 00:00:28.338
a citation,

00:00:28.738 --> 00:00:31.199
without understanding anything it produces.

00:00:32.199 --> 00:00:36.797
The legitimacy-conferring machinery runs smoothly, with nobody home.

00:00:37.297 --> 00:00:41.662
Slop University simply runs that machinery in public, under its own name.

00:00:42.862 --> 00:00:45.463
Nothing here pollutes the scholarly record.

00:00:45.863 --> 00:00:50.367
Its DOIs use the reserved test prefix, ten point five five five five,

00:00:50.667 --> 00:00:53.268
and resolve only through its own site.

00:00:54.268 --> 00:00:56.497
Nothing here impersonates anyone.

00:00:56.897 --> 00:01:00.194
The researchers are invented, and checked against real people;

00:01:00.494 --> 00:01:01.841
every image is generated.

00:01:02.841 --> 00:01:05.442
Exactly one real person appears here:

00:01:05.742 --> 00:01:08.110
the artist, as its Vice-Chancellor.

00:01:08.510 --> 00:01:12.086
He decides what the University publishes under its name,

00:01:12.386 --> 00:01:14.940
and makes no difference to the output whatsoever.

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:18.509
It is a comment about systems,

00:01:18.809 --> 00:01:21.734
and about the things those systems incentivise.
